>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a tap replacement?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything needed to swap your old tap for the new one. We take the old tap out, fit the new one, test it and take the old one away.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Turning off the water and draining the pipes to the tap</li>
        <li>Taking out the old tap, even if the nuts have seized</li>
        <li>Fitting the new tap and its flexible hoses</li>
        <li>Connecting it to your hot and cold pipes</li>
        <li>Checking the tap is firm and does not wobble</li>
        <li>Running the water and checking every joint for leaks</li>
        <li>Taking the old tap and packaging away</li>
        <li>A 12-month guarantee on our work</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We fit kitchen mixer taps, pull-out spray taps, basin mono mixers, pillar taps, bath fillers and bath shower mixers. A pair of bath taps or basin pillar taps counts as one tap.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Not included:</strong> moving the pipes, cutting a new tap hole, or changing the sink. If your job needs any of these, we tell you the price before we start.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If your tap works but looks tired, or drips again and again, replace it. If it is fairly new and only drips, a repair is usually cheaper.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Your situation</th><th>Best option</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>You have bought a new tap</td><td>Fit only</td><td>£110</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Kitchen and bathroom taps both need changing</td><td>Two taps, one visit</td><td>£160</td></tr>
            <tr><td>You do not know which tap to buy</td><td>We supply the tap</td><td>£110 + tap at cost</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tap is fairly new but drips</td><td>Repair</td><td>From £120, first hour</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tap is old, loose or keeps dripping</td><td>Replace it</td><td>£110</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Not sure? Send us a photo of the tap and the pipes under the sink. We will tell you which way is cheaper.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does a tap replacement work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Most kitchen and basin taps take about an hour, from start to finish. Bath taps can take a little longer.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Call or book online.</strong> Tell us which taps you want changed. We confirm the fixed price.</li>
        <li><strong>We check the tap.</strong> If you have bought one, we check it suits your sink and water pressure.</li>
        <li><strong>Water off.</strong> We turn off the water at the isolation valve or the stopcock.</li>
        <li><strong>Old tap out.</strong> We take out the old tap. Seized nuts are common in older homes, and we have the tools for them.</li>
        <li><strong>New tap in.</strong> We fit the new tap and connect it to the pipes. This takes about 30 minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>Test and tidy.</strong> We run the hot and cold, check for leaks, clean up and take the old tap away.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Got your new tap ready?</strong> Call and we will book the next free slot.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="buying">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What should I check before I buy a new tap?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Check three things: your water pressure, the number of tap holes in your sink, and the space under it. Getting these right saves a second trip.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Water pressure</h3>
          <p>Most modern mixers need mains pressure. That is fine with a combi boiler or an unvented cylinder. If your hot water comes from a tank in the loft, buy a tap marked for low pressure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Tap holes</h3>
          <p>A mono mixer needs one hole. Pillar taps need two. Going from two taps to one mixer? You need a new sink or a blanking plate for the spare hole.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Space under the sink</h3>
          <p>Pull-out spray taps need room for the hose. Boiling water and filter taps need room for a tank or filter, and a boiling tap needs a power socket too.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Approved for UK water</h3>
          <p>Taps must meet the UK water fittings rules. A WRAS-approved tap from a UK seller is the safest bet. Very cheap imported taps can leak and be hard to get parts for.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">Rather not choose? We can supply a good tap for you, at the price we pay for it. You still pay £110 to fit it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="dripping">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you fix a dripping or leaking tap?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Tap repairs cost £120 for the first hour on weekdays, 9am to 4pm, with no call-out fee. Most dripping taps are fixed in that first hour.</p>
      <h3>What causes a dripping tap?</h3>
      <ul class="brx-list">
        <li><strong>Worn washer.</strong> Older taps that turn several times use a rubber washer. It wears out and the tap drips.</li>
        <li><strong>Worn cartridge.</strong> Mixers and quarter-turn taps use a ceramic cartridge. When it wears, the tap drips or will not turn off fully.</li>
        <li><strong>Worn O-ring.</strong> Water around the base of the spout usually means a worn seal.</li>
        <li><strong>Leak under the sink.</strong> Often a loose or split flexible hose. Left alone, it can rot the cupboard floor.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Water pouring under the sink?</strong> Turn off the isolation valve on the pipe, or the stopcock, then call {PHONE}. We typically arrive within 30 minutes for emergencies.</p></div>
      <h3>Repair prices</h3>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>First hour, inc VAT</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Weekdays 9am to 4pm</td><td>£120</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Evenings, nights and weekends</td><td>£150</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Bank holidays</td><td>£180</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>There is no call-out fee. Parts are priced before we fit them. If the job needs more time, we tell you the price before we carry on. If a repair is not worth it, we say so, and you can switch to a new tap for £110.</p>
      <p>A leak that has soaked into a ceiling or floor may need tracing. See our <a href="/leak-detection-liverpool">leak detection</a> page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="more-jobs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you do other small jobs on the same visit?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Adding jobs to one visit saves you money. Make a list and we will give you one price before we start.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><a href="/outside-tap-installation-liverpool">Outside tap supplied and fitted</a>: £145</li>
        <li><a href="/kitchen-sink-replacement-liverpool">Kitchen sink swap</a>, like-for-like, fit only: £225</li>
        <li><a href="/gas-hob-installation-liverpool">Gas hob fitted</a> by our Gas Safe registered engineers: £120</li>
        <li><a href="/toilet-repair-liverpool">Toilet repair</a>: from £120 for the first hour</li>
        <li><a href="/radiators-liverpool">Radiator swap</a>: from £245 supplied and fitted</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Changing the kitchen sink as well? The sink swap price includes fitting the tap to the new sink. See all our fixed prices on the <a href="/small-plumbing-jobs-liverpool">small plumbing jobs</a> page.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Fitting a boiling water tap?</strong> It needs a power socket under the sink. Our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk/">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a> can fit one safely.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
